      },
      "body": "First define a NULL pointer and then increment it by 1. When accessing this pointer, an illegal instruction error occurs. Please give me some help. I have tried several methods but no work.\n\n```\n#!/bin/env bpftrace\n\nBEGIN {\n\t$p = (void *)0;\n\t$p2 = $p + 1;\n\n\t$p3 = $p2;           // OK\n\n\t$p4 = $p3 + 2;       // Illegal instruction\n\n\t@[$p2] = count();    // Illegal instruction\n\tprint($p2);          // Illegal instruction\n\tprintf(\"%p\\n\", $p2); // Illegal instruction\n}\n```",
