      },
      "body": "I tried compiling bpftrace using `./build-release.sh`, and after some wrangling I was able to have it generate a binary:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ ls -l bpftrace\r\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 joe joe 21590408 Feb  6 12:48 bpftrace\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, when running it on my host, I receive the error \"No such file or directory\"\r\n```\r\n$ ./bpftrace --help\r\n-bash: ./bpftrace: No such file or directory\r\n```\r\n```\r\n$ strace ./bpftrace --help\r\nexecve(\"./bpftrace\", [\"./bpftrace\", \"--help\"], 0x7fff87719398 /* 80 vars */) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)\r\nstrace: exec: No such file or directory\r\n+++ exited with 1 +++\r\n```\r\n```\r\n$ strace ls ./bpftrace 2>&1 | grep stat\r\nfstat(3, {st_mode=S_IFREG|0644, st_size=160647, ...}) = 0\r\nfstat(3, {st_mode=S_IFREG|0644, st_size=163240, ...}) = 0\r\nfstat(3, {st_mode=S_IFREG|0755, st_size=2025032, ...}) = 0\r\nfstat(3, {st_mode=S_IFREG|0644, st_size=539176, ...}) = 0\r\nfstat(3, {st_mode=S_IFREG|0644, st_size=18816, ...}) = 0\r\nfstat(3, {st_mode=S_IFREG|0755, st_size=158288, ...}) = 0\r\nstatfs(\"/sys/fs/selinux\", 0x7ffe304959f0) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)\r\nstatfs(\"/selinux\", 0x7ffe304959f0)      = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)\r\nfstat(3, {st_mode=S_IFREG|0444, st_size=0, ...}) = 0\r\nfstat(3, {st_mode=S_IFREG|0644, st_size=5698896, ...}) = 0\r\nstat(\"./bpftrace\", {st_mode=S_IFREG|0755, st_size=21590408, ...}) = 0\r\nlstat(\"./bpftrace\", {st_mode=S_IFREG|0755, st_size=21590408, ...}) = 0\r\nfstat(1, {st_mode=S_IFIFO|0600, st_size=0, ...}) = 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nUbuntu 19.10 eoan, using `v0.9.4` git tag from the repository.\r\n\r\nIf I exec into the container, I can execute it. Is this just a statically build binary from alpine being unable to execute on an Ubuntu system?",
