      "body": "<!--\r\nNote: bpftrace is under active development and not all distros ship the most\r\nrecent version yet. Please make sure the bug reproduces on the latest release\r\nor master.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### What reproduces the bug?\r\nwhen I run the following command, \r\n```\r\nbpftrace -e 'kprobe:consume_skb{$skb = (struct sk_buff *)arg0;$iph = ((struct iphdr *) ($skb->head + $skb->network_header));printf(\"$iph:%p\\n\",$iph);}'\r\n```\r\nI got a error: Segmentation fault (core dumped);\r\nwhat I  expect is to print ipheader pointer;\r\n\r\n#### gdb backtrace\r\nI use gdb to print the backtrace\r\n```\r\nThread 1 \"bpftrace\" received signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault.\r\nllvm::SelectionDAG::getNode (this=0x1289250, Opcode=55, DL=..., VT=..., N1=..., N2=..., Flags=...) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAG.cpp:5650\r\n5650\t    bool IsN2C = isConstantIntBuildVectorOrConstantInt(N2);\r\n(gdb) bt\r\n#0  llvm::SelectionDAG::getNode (this=0x1289250, Opcode=55, DL=..., VT=..., N1=..., N2=..., Flags=...)\r\n    at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAG.cpp:5650\r\n#1  0x00007ffff0d4d1df in llvm::DAGTypeLegalizer::PromoteIntRes_SimpleIntBinOp (this=0x7fffffff86f8, N=0x1304b90)\r\n    at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/LegalizeIntegerTypes.cpp:1194\r\n#2  llvm::DAGTypeLegalizer::PromoteIntegerResult (this=0x7fffffff86f8, N=0x1304b90, ResNo=0)\r\n    at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/LegalizeIntegerTypes.cpp:160\r\n#3  0x00007ffff0d79df5 in llvm::DAGTypeLegalizer::run (this=0x7fffffff86f8) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/LegalizeTypes.cpp:255\r\n#4  llvm::SelectionDAG::LegalizeTypes (this=<optimized out>) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/LegalizeTypes.cpp:1052\r\n#5  0x00007ffff0e7cf22 in llvm::SelectionDAGISel::CodeGenAndEmitDAG (this=0x12880b0) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAGISel.cpp:840\r\n#6  0x00007ffff0e7cd95 in llvm::SelectionDAGISel::SelectBasicBlock (this=0x129fda0, Begin=..., End=..., HadTailCall=<error reading variable: Cannot access memory at address 0x3f>)\r\n    at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAGISel.cpp:734\r\n#7  0x00007ffff0e7c500 in llvm::SelectionDAGISel::SelectAllBasicBlocks (this=0x12880b0, Fn=...)\r\n    at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAGISel.cpp:1634\r\n#8  0x00007ffff0e79849 in llvm::SelectionDAGISel::runOnMachineFunction (this=0x12880b0, mf=...) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/SelectionDAGISel.cpp:515\r\n#9  0x00007ffff09e55dd in llvm::MachineFunctionPass::runOnFunction (this=0x12880b0, F=...) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/CodeGen/MachineFunctionPass.cpp:72\r\n#10 0x00007ffff0777921 in llvm::FPPassManager::runOnFunction (this=0x7fffe80496a0, F=...) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/IR/LegacyPassManager.cpp:1434\r\n#11 0x00007ffff077e813 in llvm::FPPassManager::runOnModule (this=0x7fffe80496a0, M=...) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/IR/LegacyPassManager.cpp:1480\r\n#12 0x00007ffff0778099 in (anonymous namespace)::MPPassManager::runOnModule (this=0x7fffe80436c0, M=...) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/IR/LegacyPassManager.cpp:1549\r\n#13 llvm::legacy::PassManagerImpl::run (this=0x1285000, M=...) at /usr/src/debug/llvm-14.0.5-1.fc36.x86_64/lib/IR/LegacyPassManager.cpp:539\r\n#14 0x00000000006cd92d in bpftrace::ast::CodegenLLVM::emit (this=0x7fffffffa3c0, stream=...) at /home/barry/workspace/dynamic-tracing/ebpf/bpftrace/src/ast/passes/codegen_llvm.cpp:3306\r\n#15 0x00000000006cd9e8 in bpftrace::ast::CodegenLLVM::emit[abi:cxx11]() (this=0x7fffffffa3c0) at /home/barry/workspace/dynamic-tracing/ebpf/bpftrace/src/ast/passes/codegen_llvm.cpp:3315\r\n#16 0x000000000042164d in main (argc=3, argv=0x7fffffffcab8) at /home/barry/workspace/dynamic-tracing/ebpf/bpftrace/src/main.cpp:932\r\n(gdb) \r\n```\r\n\r\n### bpftrace --info\r\n```\r\nSystem\r\n  OS: Linux 5.19.15-201.fc36.x86_64 #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu Oct 13 18:58:38 UTC 2022\r\n  Arch: x86_64\r\n\r\nBuild\r\n  version: v0.16.0-32-gcf34\r\n  LLVM: 14.0.5\r\n  foreach_sym: yes\r\n  unsafe uprobe: no\r\n  bfd: yes\r\n  bcc_usdt_addsem: yes\r\n  bcc bpf_attach_uprobe refcount: yes\r\n  bcc library path resolution: yes\r\n  libbpf btf dump: yes\r\n  libbpf btf dump type decl: yes\r\n  libbpf bpf_prog_load: yes\r\n  libbpf bpf_map_create: yes\r\n  libdw (DWARF support): yes\r\n\r\nKernel helpers\r\n  probe_read: yes\r\n  probe_read_str: yes\r\n  probe_read_user: yes\r\n  probe_read_user_str: yes\r\n  probe_read_kernel: yes\r\n  probe_read_kernel_str: yes\r\n  get_current_cgroup_id: yes\r\n  send_signal: yes\r\n  override_return: no\r\n  get_boot_ns: yes\r\n  dpath: yes\r\n  skboutput: no\r\n\r\nKernel features\r\n  Instruction limit: 1000000\r\n  Loop support: yes\r\n  btf: yes\r\n  map batch: yes\r\n  uprobe refcount (depends on Build:bcc bpf_attach_uprobe refcount): yes\r\n\r\nMap types\r\n  hash: yes\r\n  percpu hash: yes\r\n  array: yes\r\n  percpu array: yes\r\n  stack_trace: yes\r\n  perf_event_array: yes\r\n\r\nProbe types\r\n  kprobe: yes\r\n  tracepoint: yes\r\n  perf_event: yes\r\n  kfunc: yes\r\n  iter:task: yes\r\n  iter:task_file: yes\r\n  kprobe_multi: no\r\n  raw_tp_special: yes\r\n```\r\n### my environment\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/48012058/197336946-53827967-d1f2-4a2f-bcec-f1711b36c2f4.png)\r\n\r\n",
