      "body": "<!--\r\nNote: bpftrace is under active development and not all distros ship the most\r\nrecent version yet. Please make sure the bug reproduces on the latest release\r\nor master.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### What reproduces the bug?\r\n<!--\r\nEnter details about your bug, preferably with a small code snippet.\r\n\r\nAlso describe what you expect to happen.\r\n-->\r\nOn Ubuntu 22.04, followed the installation instructions (copied from INSTALL.md):\r\n```\r\nsudo apt-get update\r\nsudo apt-get install -y \\\r\n  bison \\\r\n  cmake \\\r\n  flex \\\r\n  g++ \\\r\n  git \\\r\n  libelf-dev \\\r\n  zlib1g-dev \\\r\n  libfl-dev \\\r\n  systemtap-sdt-dev \\\r\n  binutils-dev \\\r\n  libcereal-dev \\\r\n  llvm-12-dev \\\r\n  llvm-12-runtime \\\r\n  libclang-12-dev \\\r\n  clang-12 \\\r\n  libpcap-dev \\\r\n  libgtest-dev \\\r\n  libgmock-dev \\\r\n  asciidoctor\r\ngit clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/iovisor/bpftrace\r\nmkdir bpftrace/build; cd bpftrace/build;\r\n../build-libs.sh\r\ncmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release ..\r\nmake -j8\r\nsudo make install\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe problem:\r\n```\r\n$ bpftrace --info\r\n$ bpftrace: /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libbpf.so.0: version `LIBBPF_0.6.0' not found (required by bpftrace)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### bpftrace --info\r\nSee above\r\n",
