      "body": "<!--\nNote: bpftrace is under active development and not all distros ship the most\nrecent version yet. Please make sure the bug reproduces on the latest release\nor master.\n-->\n\n### What reproduces the bug? Provide code if possible.\n\nTrying to track down an issue in PostgreSQL 17 I tried to use the following script:\n\n```\nuprobe:/usr/lib/postgresql/17/bin/postgres:MemoryContextSizeFailure {\n  printf(\"%s: size=%lu, flags=%d\\n\", func, (uint64) arg1, (int32) arg2);\n  @failed[tid] = true;\n  print(ustack);\n}\n\nuprobe:/usr/lib/postgresql/17/bin/postgres:ReorderBufferAddInvalidations {\n  @size[tid] = arg3;\n}\n\nuretprobe:/usr/lib/postgresql/17/bin/postgres:ReorderBufferAddInvalidations /@failed[tid]/ {\n  printf(\"%s: size=%lu\\n\", func, (uint64) @size[tid]);\n}\n```\n\nIdea is to print out caller information on a call to `MemoryContextSizeFailure`.\n\nHowever, when executing it, it fails with\n\n```\nmats@fury:~/research/ebpf/postgres$ sudo bpftrace trace-mcxt.bt\nAttaching 3 probes...\nERROR: failed to create map: '@failed': Too many open files\nERROR: failed to create map: '@size': Too many open files\nERROR: failed to create stack id map: Too many open files\nERROR: This might have happened because kernel.perf_event_max_stack is smaller than 127. Try to tweak this value with sysctl kernel.perf_event_max_stack=<new value>\nERROR: failed to create  map: Too many open files\nERROR: failed to create map: 'ringbuf_loss_counter': Too many open files\nCreation of the required BPF maps has failed.\nMake sure you have all the required permissions and are not confined (e.g. like\nsnapcraft does). `dmesg` will likely have useful output for further troubleshooting\n```\n\nRemoving all probes but the probe on `MemoryContextSizeFailure` allow it to execute and print the stack for this case.\n### `bpftrace --info` output\n\n```\nSystem\n  OS: Linux 6.8.0-62-generic #65-Ubuntu SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon May 19 17:15:03 UTC 2025\n  Arch: x86_64\n\nBuild\n  version: v0.20.2\n  LLVM: 18.1.3\n  unsafe probe: no\n  bfd: no\n  libdw (DWARF support): yes\n\nKernel helpers\n  probe_read: yes\n  probe_read_str: yes\n  probe_read_user: yes\n  probe_read_user_str: yes\n  probe_read_kernel: yes\n  probe_read_kernel_str: yes\n  get_current_cgroup_id: yes\n  send_signal: yes\n  override_return: yes\n  get_boot_ns: yes\n  dpath: no\n  skboutput: no\n  get_tai_ns: yes\n  get_func_ip: yes\n  jiffies64: yes\n\nKernel features\n  Instruction limit: 1000000\n  Loop support: yes\n  btf: yes\n  module btf: yes\n  map batch: yes\n  uprobe refcount (depends on Build:bcc bpf_attach_uprobe refcount): yes\n\nMap types\n  hash: yes\n  percpu hash: yes\n  array: yes\n  percpu array: yes\n  stack_trace: yes\n  perf_event_array: yes\n  ringbuf: yes\n\nProbe types\n  kprobe: yes\n  tracepoint: yes\n  perf_event: yes\n  kfunc: yes\n  kprobe_multi: yes\n  uprobe_multi: yes\n  raw_tp_special: yes\n  iter: yes\n```",
      "reactions": {
