      },
      "body": "```\r\nStarting program: /usr/local/bin/bpftrace -e BEGIN\\ \\{\\ @=\\*uptr\\(kaddr\\(\\\"do_poweroff\\\"\\)\\)\\ \\} -kk\r\nAttaching 1 probe...\r\nstdin:1:9-12: WARNING: Failed to probe_read_user: Bad address (-14)\r\nBEGIN { @=*uptr(kaddr(\"do_poweroff\")) }\r\n        ~~~\r\n\r\nThread 1 \"bpftrace\" received signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault.\r\n0x00007fffee622858 in std::__cxx11::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char> >::basic_string(std::__cxx11::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char> > const&) () from /lib64/libstdc++.so.6\r\nMissing separate debuginfos, use: dnf debuginfo-install bcc-0.15.0-2.fc32.x86_64 clang-libs-10.0.1-3.fc32.x86_64 elfutils-libelf-0.182-1.fc32.x86_64 libbpf-0.0.7-1.fc32.x86_64 libedit-3.1-32.20191231cvs.fc32.x86_64 libffi-3.1-24.fc32.x86_64 libgcc-10.2.1-9.fc32.x86_64 libstdc++-10.2.1-9.fc32.x86_64 llvm-libs-10.0.1-4.fc32.x86_64 ncurses-libs-6.1-15.20191109.fc32.x86_64 zlib-1.2.11-21.fc32.x86_64\r\n(gdb) bt\r\n#0  0x00007fffee622858 in std::__cxx11::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char> >::basic_string(std::__cxx11::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char> > const&) () from /lib64/libstdc++.so.6\r\n#1  0x000000000045e91c in bpftrace::perf_event_printer (cb_cookie=0x7fffffffa9e0,\r\n    data=0x7fffeb2a400c, size=20) at /vagrant/src/bpftrace.cpp:594\r\n#2  0x00007ffff7607f56 in perf_reader_event_read () from /lib64/libbcc.so.0\r\n#3  0x0000000000462614 in bpftrace::BPFtrace::poll_perf_events (this=0x7fffffffa9e0,\r\n    epollfd=5, drain=false) at /vagrant/src/bpftrace.cpp:1148\r\n#4  0x0000000000461c7a in bpftrace::BPFtrace::run (this=0x7fffffffa9e0,\r\n    bpforc=std::unique_ptr<bpftrace::BpfOrc> = {...})\r\n    at /vagrant/src/bpftrace.cpp:1067\r\n#5  0x000000000050b38c in main (argc=4, argv=0x7fffffffe428)\r\n    at /vagrant/src/main.cpp:878\r\n```\r\n\r\nBuilt from master(853142ac7883662cfb8ccb6566400dd7a88c7be9) in the fed32 box, commit id mismatches as I'm 3 docs commits ahead.\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ sudo bpftrace --info\r\nSystem\r\n  OS: Linux 5.6.6-300.fc32.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Apr 21 13:44:19 UTC 2020\r\n  Arch: x86_64\r\n\r\nBuild\r\n  version: v0.11.0-370-gc1d53-dirty\r\n  LLVM: 10.0.1\r\n  foreach_sym: yes\r\n  unsafe uprobe: no\r\n  bfd: yes\r\n  bpf_attach_kfunc: yes\r\n  bcc_usdt_addsem: yes\r\n  bcc bpf_attach_uprobe refcount: no\r\n  libbpf: yes\r\n  libbpf btf dump: yes\r\n  libbpf btf dump type decl: yes\r\n```",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/1712/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
