      "issue_field_values": [

      ],
      "type": {
        "id": 82712,
        "node_id": "IT_kwDOCWTeF84AAUMY",
        "name": "Bug",
        "description": "An unexpected problem or behavior",
        "color": "red",
        "created_at": "2024-01-24T13:01:17Z",
        "updated_at": "2024-07-26T10:04:48Z",
        "is_enabled": true
      },
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "sub_issues_summary": {
        "total": 0,
        "completed": 0,
        "percent_completed": 0
      },
      "issue_dependencies_summary": {
        "blocked_by": 0,
        "total_blocked_by": 0,
        "blocking": 0,
        "total_blocking": 0
      },
      "body": "It looks like the fix for #12 introduced a fairly serious regression when parsing invalid probe names:\r\n\r\n```\r\n> gdb -q /usr/local/bin/bpftrace.new\r\nReading symbols from /usr/local/bin/bpftrace.new...done.\r\n(gdb) set args -e 'bad:probe:name { exit(); }'\r\n(gdb) run\r\nStarting program: /usr/local/bin/bpftrace.new -e 'bad:probe:name { exit(); }'\r\nMissing separate debuginfos, use: debuginfo-install glibc-2.17-222.el7.x86_64\r\n[Thread debugging using libthread_db enabled]\r\nUsing host libthread_db library \"/lib64/libthread_db.so.1\".\r\n\r\nProgram received signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault.\r\n0x00007ffff2db3f63 in std::string::size() const () from /lib64/libstdc++.so.6\r\nMissing separate debuginfos, use: debuginfo-install devtoolset-6-elfutils-libelf-0.167-2.el7.x86_64 libedit-3.0-12.20121213cvs.el7.x86_64 libgcc-4.8.5-28.el7_5.1.x86_64 libstdc++-4.8.5-28.el7_5.1.x86_64 libxml2-2.9.1-6.el7_2.3.x86_64 ncurses-libs-5.9-14.20130511.el7_4.x86_64 xz-libs-5.2.2-1.el7.x86_64 zlib-1.2.7-17.el7.x86_64\r\n(gdb) bt\r\n#0  0x00007ffff2db3f63 in std::string::size() const () from /lib64/libstdc++.so.6\r\n#1  0x000000000051f660 in std::operator==<char> (__lhs=\"bad\",\r\n    __rhs=<error reading variable: Cannot access memory at address 0xffffffffffffffe8>)\r\n    at /opt/rh/devtoolset-6/root/usr/include/c++/6.2.1/bits/basic_string.h:5060\r\n#2  0x000000000057dbe2 in bpftrace::probetypeName (type=\"bad\") at /data/users/jonhaslam/bpftrace/src/types.cpp:70\r\n#3  0x00000000005b7672 in bpftrace::ast::SemanticAnalyser::visit (this=0x7fffffffd2a0, ap=...)\r\n    at /data/users/jonhaslam/bpftrace/src/ast/semantic_analyser.cpp:686\r\n#4  0x00000000005800b2 in bpftrace::ast::AttachPoint::accept (this=0x8a20a0, v=...)\r\n    at /data/users/jonhaslam/bpftrace/src/ast/ast.cpp:68\r\n#5  0x00000000005b84c7 in bpftrace::ast::SemanticAnalyser::visit (this=0x7fffffffd2a0, probe=...)\r\n    at /data/users/jonhaslam/bpftrace/src/ast/semantic_analyser.cpp:799\r\n#6  0x000000000058014c in bpftrace::ast::Probe::accept (this=0x8a2200, v=...)\r\n    at /data/users/jonhaslam/bpftrace/src/ast/ast.cpp:80\r\n#7  0x00000000005b8612 in bpftrace::ast::SemanticAnalyser::visit (this=0x7fffffffd2a0, program=...)\r\n    at /data/users/jonhaslam/bpftrace/src/ast/semantic_analyser.cpp:813\r\n#8  0x0000000000580180 in bpftrace::ast::Program::accept (this=0x8a2270, v=...)\r\n    at /data/users/jonhaslam/bpftrace/src/ast/ast.cpp:84\r\n#9  0x00000000005b868d in bpftrace::ast::SemanticAnalyser::analyse (this=0x7fffffffd2a0)\r\n    at /data/users/jonhaslam/bpftrace/src/ast/semantic_analyser.cpp:822\r\n#10 0x0000000000571161 in main (argc=3, argv=0x7fffffffdb58) at /data/users/jonhaslam/bpftrace/src/main.cpp:169\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe walk off the end of the array when we don't match a probe as 'sizeof(PROBE_LIST)' returns the size in bytes of the PROBE_LIST array and not the number of elements as was intended.\r\n\r\nThe fix is to either simply do 'sizeof(PROBE_LIST) / sizeof(*PROBE_LIST)' or, preferably, use a container type such as 'std::vector'.\r\n\r\nTests should also be added to catch this regression.\r\n",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/231/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
        "+1": 0,
        "-1": 0,
