      "body": "Following a [guide from the Reference](https://github.com/iovisor/bpftrace/blob/master/docs/tutorial_one_liners.md#lesson-3-file-opens) I get a distorted output for filename param. I've tried playing with my Konsole encoding settings (set to Unicode by default), but no effect.\r\n\r\nExample output:\r\n\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!��t(�V:\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!��t(�V:\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!��h\r\n>                               �V:\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!�����V:\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!�PI �V:\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!�@�}�V:\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!�@�}�V:\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!�@�}�V:\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!��u��V:\r\n> Chrome_IOThread         !�!��u��V:\r\n> brave ���\r\n> konsole ��_\r\n> konsole ��_\r\n> konsole `�_\r\n> konsole ��_\r\n> konsole ��_\r\n> krusader  qE��U\r\n\r\n### What reproduces the bug?\r\n```bash\r\n# bpftrace -e 'tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_openat { printf(\"%s %s\\n\", comm, str(args->filename)); }'\r\n```\r\nI expect to see the actual file names.\r\n\r\n### \r\n\r\n# bpftrace --info\r\n```bash\r\nroot@jrmpc:~# bpftrace --info\r\nbpftrace: invalid option -- '-'\r\nUSAGE:\r\n    bpftrace [options] filename\r\n    bpftrace [options] -e 'program'\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n    -d             debug info dry run\r\n    -dd            verbose debug info dry run\r\n    -e 'program'   execute this program\r\n    -h             show this help message\r\n    -l [search]    list probes\r\n    -p PID         enable USDT probes on PID\r\n    -c 'CMD'       run CMD and enable USDT probes on resulting process\r\n    -v             verbose messages\r\n\r\nENVIRONMENT:\r\n    BPFTRACE_STRLEN    [default: 64] bytes on BPF stack per str()\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES:\r\nbpftrace -l '*sleep*'\r\n    list probes containing \"sleep\"\r\nbpftrace -e 'kprobe:do_nanosleep { printf(\"PID %d sleeping...\\n\", pid); }'\r\n    trace processes calling sleep\r\nbpftrace -e 'tracepoint:raw_syscalls:sys_enter { @[comm] = count(); }'\r\n    count syscalls by process name\r\n```",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/1699/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
        "+1": 0,
        "-1": 0,
