      },
      "body": "As @Birch-san  raised in https://github.com/iovisor/bpftrace/discussions/1785 and https://github.com/iovisor/bpftrace/discussions/1782 our development proces is a bit annoying. \r\n\r\nWith the release of LLVM12 I think its time to update our dev setup to LLVM12 only. Most distros have already moved away from llvm7 and 8-11 have the stack reuse bug so 12 seems like our best option.\r\n\r\nI don't think we really need to test all these versions, our codegen is still pretty much the same between all versions. We might have a API rename, but no completely different logic.\r\n\r\nThat would mean our codegen and codegen validator tests would be LLVM 12 only. Support for all other versions can be dropped (just don't run the tests).\r\n\r\nIt's a bit of churn but afterwards we can ignore it again for 1.5/2y (hopefully)\r\n\r\n@danobi @Birch-san @olsajiri @viktormalik  thoughts?\r\n",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/1797/reactions",
