      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "draft": false,
      "pull_request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/pulls/1063",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/1063",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/1063.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/1063.patch",
        "merged_at": "2020-05-15T08:23:20Z"
      },
      "body": "This picks up where #867 and #917 left off and builds on their insights. The versions of Alpine and bcc that we're currently using are a bit old. A static package for bcc is now available in Alpine's `edge` repository, and it should significantly reduce our CI build times by avoiding an expensive compilation step.\r\n\r\nFor unclear reasons, the `ast` build target is including `-Wl,-Bdynamic /usr/lib/llvm8/lib/libLLVM-8.so` in the link step, which causes the static initialization failure and segfault noted [here](https://github.com/iovisor/bpftrace/pull/867#issuecomment-537624591). The problem seems to stem from `clang_libs` [0], but I spent a couple hours experimenting with cmake options and couldn't find a solution. I've left the sed hack from #867 in place to handle this for now.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately the header parsing crashes noted in #266 are still happening with llvm8 and a newer BCC. A few of the unit and runtime tests are failing with similar errors for me locally when I use the static build. Seems like more evidence that it's an issue specific to musl.\r\n\r\nFWIW, I feel like the approach outlined in #1041 is better for the long term, but maybe this can improve CI in the meantime.\r\n\r\nThanks to @sezuan, @danobi, and others for the earlier work on this.\r\n\r\n-------\r\n\r\n[0] You can \"box in\" the link options in the build output using something like this -- start-group and end-group can be any valid flag -- which suggested to me that `clang_libs` is involved in the incorrect linking:\r\n\r\n```\r\ntarget_link_libraries(ast -Wl,--start-group ${clang_libs} -Wl,--end-group)\r\n```\r\n\r\nlibLLVM-8.so will appear at the end of the group.",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/1063/reactions",
